SSE inline fast path: scalar and packed float on the host FPU (doc 16).

Every SSE float instruction was a helper call into softfloat (hardfloat
once PE is sticky, but still a call and a lane loop). This patch
translates the common cases inline when MXCSR admits the host FPU
verbatim (RC nearest, no FTZ/DAZ, all exceptions masked, property
sse-fast on) AND the precision flag is already sticky in env->sse_status
(TB flag bit 31): then an admissible operation can raise nothing but PE,
so the inline code only classifies its result (operands for compares)
and takes the unmodified helper out of line otherwise, bit- and
flag-exact against softfloat. ldmxcsr/fxrstor/xrstor end the TB; a TB
translated before PE was sticky exits after the helper that sets it.

TCG grows scalar binary32 opcodes (add/sub/mul/div/sqrt_f32 on i32
temps in vector registers), int32 <-> float conversions, and vector
float opcodes (fadd/fsub/fmul/fdiv/fsqrt_vec, MO_32/MO_64) in the
aarch64 and x86-64 backends. Packed instructions run on the vector unit
with vector checks and one lane-mask branch; scalar ones in general
registers. Inlined: add, sub, mul, div, min, max, sqrt (ps/pd/ss/sd),
rcp, rsqrt (ps/ss), cmp with the 8 legacy predicates, comis/ucomis,
cvt(t)ss2si, cvt(t)sd2si, cvtsi2ss/sd, cvtss2sd, cvtsd2ss. Legacy
encodings only. Slow blocks share x87-shadow's array and emitter.

Test: tools/sse-guest-test.py (DOS program, 61 sequences x every pair
of 47 single / 33 double edge values x 3 MXCSR settings, 333,875 result
lines identical on/off on the M1 Air). Register-only bench: packed 12x,
scalar 3.6x over the helpers. x86-64 backend code is untested (no host).
